IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PARTS 1 AND 1A: regulation 1 (citation, commencement, application and
-- interpretation) and regulation 1A (full rate of state pension).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
--
-- Pensionable age is never worked out here: it is fixed by the Pensions Act 1995,
-- which is not among the inputs, so every rule that needs it takes the DATE on which
-- the person reaches (or reached) pensionable age as a plain input.

§ `Part 1: General`

§§ `Regulation 1(1): citation`

-- Regulation 1(1) gives the Regulations their short title. It decides nothing for
-- a person, so it is inert (NOTES.md, coverage table).

§§ `Regulation 1(2): commencement`

-- src:14 | (2) These Regulations come into force on 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 1(2) (src:14)
`regulation 1(2): the commencement date` MEANS YMD 2016 4 6

§§ `Regulation 1(3): who the Regulations apply to`

-- Gloss: "pensionable age" is the age at which a person becomes able to claim the
-- state pension; it is fixed by other legislation (not in the inputs), so the
-- date on which the person reaches it is taken as an input.
-- Part 5 (regulation 14 and the Schedule) is the exception and applies whatever
-- the person's pensionable age date: see `regulation 1(3): Part 5 applies to the person`.
-- src:15 | (3) These Regulations (except Part 5) do not apply to a person who reaches pensionable age before 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 1(3) (src:15)
GIVEN `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 1(3): these Regulations (except Part 5) apply to the person` MEANS
    NOT (`the date the person reaches pensionable age` LESS THAN `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`)

-- The words "(except Part 5)" mean Part 5 is not subject to the exclusion: it applies
-- to a person whenever they reach pensionable age.
@ref Regulation 1(3) (src:15)
GIVEN `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 1(3): Part 5 applies to the person` MEANS TRUE

§§ `Regulation 1(4): interpretation`

-- The opening words of paragraph (4) are shown in the text as repealed
-- ("{repealed: In these Regulations, ...}"); the definitions follow it.
-- "the 1965 Act" and "the 2014 Act" are only names for Acts that are not inputs.
-- "deferral period" is the record DeferralPeriod in spr-nouns.l4.
-- "graduated retirement benefit" is encoded below as a test on which provision of
-- the 1965 Act the benefit is paid under.

DECLARE BenefitUnder1965Act IS ONE OF
    `a benefit under section 36 of the 1965 Act`
    `a benefit under section 37 of the 1965 Act`
    `a benefit under another provision`

-- src:21 | “graduated retirement benefit” means any benefit under section 36 (graduated retirement benefit) or 37 (special provisions as to graduated retirement benefit for widows) of the 1965 Act.
@ref Regulation 1(4), "graduated retirement benefit" (src:21)
GIVEN benefit IS A BenefitUnder1965Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 1(4): the benefit is graduated retirement benefit` benefit MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `a benefit under section 36 of the 1965 Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a benefit under section 37 of the 1965 Act` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Regulation 1(5): people treated as not married to each other`

-- Gloss: if either of two spouses is married to a third person at the time in
-- question, the two are treated as not married to each other at that time.
-- The paragraph speaks of marriage only. It says nothing of a civil partner who
-- is in a civil partnership with a third person, so a civil partnership is taken
-- as it stands (NOTES.md, fork F9).
DECLARE KindOfRelationship IS ONE OF
    `married to each other`
    `civil partners of each other`

-- src:22 | (5) For the purposes of these Regulations (except this paragraph), two people are to be treated as if they are not married to each other in relation to times when either of them is married to a third person.
@ref Regulation 1(5) (src:22)
GIVEN kind IS A KindOfRelationship
      `either of them is married to a third person at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 1(5): the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners at the time` kind `either of them is married to a third person at the time` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `married to each other` THEN NOT (`either of them is married to a third person at the time`)
    WHEN `civil partners of each other` THEN TRUE

§ `Part 1A: Full rate of State Pension`

-- Regulation 1A states a figure. The figure is that of the revised text at
-- 2026-04-06; earlier and later editions of regulation 1A carry other figures
-- (NOTES.md, fork F10), so this constant is not valid for any other date.
-- src:25 | The full rate of the state pension for the purposes of section 3(1) of the 2014 Act (full rate of state pension) is £241.30 per week.
@ref Regulation 1A (src:25)
`regulation 1A: the full rate of the state pension, in pounds per week` MEANS 241.30
